{"data":{"repository":{"issueOrPullRequest":{"__typename":"Issue","number":14822,"updatedAt":"2026-11-13T13:44:15Z","createdAt":"2026-10-26T04:50:39Z","lastEditedAt":null,"body":"## Symptom\n\n`gh run view RUN --job JOB --log-failed` fails before fetching logs for a completed organization-required workflow run:\n\n```\nfailed to get run: HTTP 404: Not Found (https://api.github.com/repos/ORG/CONSUMER/actions/workflows/WORKFLOW_ID)\n```\n\nThe same authenticated CLI can read the run metadata and download that job's logs directly. The workflow is required by an organization ruleset and originates in a shared workflow repository, rather than a workflow file in the consumer checkout.\n\n## Repro\n\n1. Configure a ruleset-required workflow from a shared repository and let its run complete for a consumer PR.\n2. Obtain the run/job IDs from the PR check URL.\n3. Run `gh run view RUN --repo ORG/CONSUMER --job JOB --log-failed`; it fails on the consumer repository's workflow metadata lookup above.\n4. With the same authentication, `gh api repos/ORG/CONSUMER/actions/runs/RUN` succeeds, and `gh api --allow-escape-sequences repos/ORG/CONSUMER/actions/jobs/JOB/logs > job.log` succeeds. In the observed case the latter retrieved 81,118 bytes. Escape sequences were captured to a file, not printed to the terminal.\n\nThe run metadata's `workflow_id` is the ID in the failing URL, and `path` is `.github/workflows/review-gate.yml`. Repository/run IDs are redacted because this reproduction originated in application development.\n\n## Expected\n\nAn explicit job-log request can read available job logs even when the optional workflow metadata lookup returns 404, or explains this workflow-source limitation without implying the run itself cannot be read.\n\n## Environment\n\n- `gh version 2.103.1 (2026-10-23)`\n- macOS 27.0\n- Observed 2026-10-26 while diagnosing a failed required review check.\n\nI searched this tracker for required-workflow/run-view and workflow/not-found/log combinations before filing.\n","author":{"__typename":"User","login":"henrymodisett"},"comments":{"totalCount":5,"nodes":[{"author":{"__typename":"Bot","login":"cli-triage"},"createdAt":"2026-10-26T04:55:38Z","lastEditedAt":null,"body":"Thanks for the detailed repro. I traced this through the source and the cause looks clear: `shared.GetRun` ([shared.go lines 559–592 at commit 4f2cfe9](https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/4f2cfe92e3499f8581bf39db77e0a1431fa7b55c/pkg/cmd/run/shared/shared.go#L559-L592)) always calls `workflowShared.GetWorkflow(client, repo, result.WorkflowID)` right after fetching the run, and returns any error from that call unmodified. For a run whose workflow originates from an organization/enterprise ruleset rather than the consumer repo's own workflow list, that lookup 404s, so `GetRun` fails before `view.go`'s `--log`/`--log-failed` path ever reaches `getRunLog`/job-log fetching — even though the run and job metadata and logs are otherwise readable. This matches a known pattern already handled more leniently elsewhere: `preloadWorkflowNames` ([shared.go lines ~487–505](https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/4f2cfe92e3499f8581bf39db77e0a1431fa7b55c/pkg/cmd/run/shared/shared.go#L478-L505)) explicitly catches a 404 from the same `GetWorkflow` call for `run list` and falls back to an empty workflow name instead of failing, but `GetRun` (used by `run view`) has no equivalent fallback. I'm suggesting `bug`, `gh-run`, and `priority-3` (narrow case with a viable `gh api` workaround) for maintainer review. This is not a duplicate of #9228 (which is about `run list`/`run view` generally 404ing on ruleset workflows); this issue is specifically about `--log-failed`/`--log` failing even though job logs themselves are fetchable, so a first responder may want to consider making `GetRun`'s workflow-name lookup tolerate a 404 the same way `preloadWorkflowNames` does.\n\n> Generated by [Issue Triage (skills-driven)](https://github.com/cli/cli/actions/runs/40271133700) for #14822 · copilot · auto · 79 AIC · ⊞ 4.5K · [◷](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Acli%2Fcli+%22gh-aw-workflow-call-id%3A+cli%2Fcli%2Fissue-triage%22&type=issues)\n\n<!-- gh-aw-agentic-workflow: Issue Triage (skills-driven), engine: copilot, model: auto, id: 40271133700, workflow_id: issue-triage, run: https://github.com/cli/cli/actions/runs/40271133700 -->\n<!-- gh-aw-workflow-call-id: cli/cli/issue-triage -->","isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":null},{"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"duongynhi000005-oss"},"createdAt":"2026-10-26T06:55:59Z","lastEditedAt":null,"body":"### Analysis & Proposed Fix\n\nIn `pkg/cmd/run/shared/shared.go`, `GetRun` always calls `workflowShared.GetWorkflow(client, repo, result.WorkflowID)` after fetching the run and returns any error from that lookup directly:\n\n```go\nworkflow, err := workflowShared.GetWorkflow(client, repo, result.WorkflowID)\nif err != nil {\n    return nil, err\n} else {\n    result.workflowName = workflow.Name\n}\n```\n\nWhen a workflow run originates from an organization or enterprise ruleset rather than a workflow file in the consumer repository, `GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/workflows/{workflow_id}` returns `404 Not Found` even though the run metadata and job logs are readable in the consumer repository. Consequently, `gh run view RUN --job JOB --log-failed` fails in `GetRun` before reaching `getRunLog`.\n\nNotably, `preloadWorkflowNames` in the same file (`pkg/cmd/run/shared/shared.go:460-474`) already handles this exact ruleset-workflow case for `gh run list` by catching `api.HTTPError` with status `404` and falling back to an empty workflow name.\n\n#### Proposed Changes\n1. **`pkg/cmd/run/shared/shared.go` (`GetRun`)**:\n   - Check `var httpErr api.HTTPError` when `workflowShared.GetWorkflow` returns an error; if `errors.As(err, &httpErr) && httpErr.StatusCode == http.StatusNotFound`, fall back to an empty `workflowName` instead of failing `GetRun`.\n2. **Tests**:\n   - Added `TestGetRunWorkflow404` in `pkg/cmd/run/shared/shared_test.go`.\n   - Added `noninteractive with job log-failed when workflow metadata returns 404 (#14822)` in `pkg/cmd/run/view/view_test.go`.\n\nI have verified this fix with `go test ./pkg/cmd/run/...` on my fork (`duongynhi000005-oss/cli-2:fix/run-view-workflow-404`, commit `1f1cb05`) and would be happy to open a PR if you'd like to assign this issue to me.","isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"SPAM"},{"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"henrymodisett"},"createdAt":"2026-10-26T10:52:28Z","lastEditedAt":null,"body":"Additional reproduction on `gh 2.103.1` (macOS), while diagnosing a required shared `validate` workflow for a merge-group candidate: `gh run view RUN --log-failed` also fails on the consumer repository's workflow-metadata endpoint with HTTP 404. The same authenticated `gh api .../actions/jobs/JOB/logs --allow-escape-sequences` successfully retrieved the job log to a file. This occurs for validation as well as the review-gate case above; no separate issue filed.\n","isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":null},{"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"henrymodisett"},"createdAt":"2026-10-30T00:53:52Z","lastEditedAt":null,"body":"Additional reproduction on the same environment: `gh run view RUN --repo ORG/CONSUMER --json jobs` also fails at the shared required workflow metadata lookup with HTTP 404 while the run is in progress. With the same authentication, `gh api repos/ORG/CONSUMER/actions/runs/RUN/jobs` succeeds and returns current job states. This is therefore not limited to completed runs or log requests. No private repository/run identifiers are included here.\n","isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":null},{"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"henrymodisett"},"createdAt":"2026-11-13T13:44:15Z","lastEditedAt":null,"body":"Reproduced on `gh version 2.104.0 (2026-11-12)` on macOS while reading a completed ruleset-required validation job on November 13. `gh run view RUN --repo ORG/CONSUMER --job JOB --log-failed` still fails at the consumer workflow-metadata endpoint with HTTP 404. The same authenticated `gh api repos/ORG/CONSUMER/actions/jobs/JOB/logs --allow-escape-sequences > job.log` succeeds; terminal sequences were captured to a file and stripped before inspection. This is the existing validation/log-fetch case on the newer release, not a separate issue. Private repository and run identifiers are omitted.\n","isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":null}]}}}}}